    "norm": "Tests that variable-name substitution is disabled by default. <p> When a template contains a nested variable expression such as {@code ${animal.${species}}}, the substitutor does NOT resolve the inner {@code ${species}} first and then use the result as part of the outer variable name. Instead, the entire outer expression is left unchanged. Simple (non-nested) variables such as {@code ${target}} are still resolved normally. </p>"
   },
